# Price-time priority walkthrough (used in the README).
# Three asks: 101 first, then two at the better price 100.
L S 1 101 5
L S 2 100 5
L S 3 100 5
# A bid for 12 @ 101 takes 2 (5), then 3 (5) at 100 — same price, earlier first —
# then 2 lots of order 1 at 101. Trades print at the maker's price.
L B 10 101 12
# Non-crossing bid rests.
L B 11 99 4
# Market sell for 10: fills 4 against bid 11 @ 99, the remaining 6 is cancelled (IOC).
M S 12 10
# Cancel the rest of order 1, then try again (unknown).
C 1
C 1
# Rejections never change the book.
L B 13 99 0
L B 14 98 1
L S 14 105 1
L B 15 0 1
# Ids are unique among *resting* orders only: order 2 was fully filled, so its id is free.
L B 2 97 1
